bool i_showLabels      = true
// ── THE SIZE CONTROL IS BACK ON THE PANEL (Aaron, 2026-07-31) ──
// It was removed earlier the same day on the reading that "the level tag size should be
// tiny" meant lock it there. It did not — Tiny is the DEFAULT wanted, not the only
// option, and those are different things. So the input returns unchanged, still
// defaulting to Tiny.
// The rest of the history stands and is why the list is only two long. Normal / Large /
// Huge were dropped on 2026-07-30: up to fifteen of these tags stack down the right
// edge, and past Small they collide with each other and with the price scale — the
// collision-avoidance pass below can only push labels apart VERTICALLY, it cannot make
// them narrower, so the big sizes produced a wall of text over the candles. Tiny for a
// laptop, Small for a large monitor.
// ONE control for every price-level tag on the right-hand side, deliberately. Sizing
// them per-tool is what makes that edge look ragged.
string liqLabelSize    = input.string("Tiny", "Level tag size", options = ["Tiny", "Small"], group = GRP_TOOLS, tooltip = "One size for every price-level tag down the right-hand side: the Liquidity Levels (PDH/PDL, PWH/PWL, PWC, H4 H/L, session highs and lows), the MV line, and the EQH/EQL pools. Deliberately ONE control — sizing them separately is what makes the right edge look ragged.", display = display.none)
bool i_currentDayOnly  = true   // always hide mitigated on new day

// Two branches now the other three options are gone. The `else` also absorbs a chart
// saved with the OLD input still storing "Normal"/"Large"/"Huge" — it falls to small
// rather than to a size that is no longer offered.
f_liqSize() =>
    liqLabelSize == "Tiny" ? size.tiny : size.small

